 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Start with the biggest issues. Loose wood rotting, cracks in the grout or cracked tiles? Those are the ones you'd notice first. Those need to be replaced with new, pressure treated pine or cedar. Yes, once the new boards are in, paint the whole deck with a marine grade exterior stain. It keeps the wood looking good and helps it rot. Two weekends would be plenty. Start with the soft boards, and if it' warm enough, give the grout and tile a quick brush over too.",
